              "note_id": "FCT_0382",
              "exact_quote": "A for loop in Java consists of three parts: an initialization statement, a boolean condition, and an increment statement."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0387",
              "exact_quote": "The for loop execution steps are: initialize the loop variable, evaluate the condition, execute the body if true, then increment the loop variable, and repeat."
            }
